Laying the answer out.

What the tools cost

The read tool is cheap and bash is not,
so the order matters. A run looks like
this:

func main() {
    fmt.Println("hello")
}

• read first, and read widely
• run only what the reading could not
  answer
  • a nested point, to show the indent

┌──────┬────────────────────────┬──────┐
│ Tool │ What it does           │ Cost │
├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
│ read │ takes a file and hands │    1 │
│      │ it back                │      │
├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
│ grep │ walks the tree looking │    4 │
│      │ for a pattern          │      │
├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
│ bash │ runs a command in a    │   40 │
│      │ sandbox with no        │      │
│      │ network                │      │
└──────┴────────────────────────┴──────┘

┌──────┐     ┌──────┐
│      │     │      │
│ read ├────►│ bash │
│      │     │      │
└──────┘     └──────┘

│ The costs are made up, and the table
│ is here to be watched as it draws.

